perate a data center in India. The company was formerly known as Atlantic Crypto Corporation and changed its name to CoreWeave, Inc. in December 2019. CoreWeave, Inc. was incorporated in 2017 and is based in Livingston, New Jersey.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Michael N. Intrator | Co-founder, President, CEO & Chairman | Age 55 | Compensation: $3.5M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 2K people. Revenue per employee of $2.3M ranks in the top quartile among Technology peers. Stock-based compensation of $288K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 1\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (7/10).","financial_summary":["CoreWeave, Inc. is a large-cap technology business with a $24.6B market cap on $5.1B of annual revenue.","Returns on capital run at -0% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The company is burning through $7.3B of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 7.6\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin -0.0\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and stock-based comp at 12% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insiders hold 18% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.1) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (27.5% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $13.1M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Carries more leverage than most Technology peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the inevitable bad year","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"58% of recent news is bearish \u2014 worth reading before sizing","sev":"amber","cat":"news"},{"text":"Technology sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 9% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Technology ETF trading well below its long-term trend","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Elevated sector volatility (52% annualized) adds uncertainty","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cybersecurity liability and talent cost inflation \u2014 a single breach can erase years of goodwill, and the war for engineering talent compresses margins even at scale.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"CoreWeave Eyes $4.5B Loan, but Bankruptcy Odds Rise to 21% on Prediction Markets","source":"benzinga.com","link":"https://www.benzinga.com/markets/prediction-markets/26/11/63685963/coreweave-wall-street-loan-bankruptcy","date":"2026-11-27","timestamp":1795804208.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Micron CEO Expects Memory Shortages to Worsen in 2028, but TrendForce Sees Prices Falling","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/micron-ceo-expects-memory-shortages-181506972.html","date":"2026-11-27",